From 9fafbcb8e9958fe05df345fe37ce0cf0dda66a2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 13:38:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(ml): MNN CPU session backend for facial recognition
 models

Adds an MnnSession that runs the face detector and the face recogniser
(and, optionally, the CLIP text tower) on MNN's CPU backend as a drop-in
replacement for the ONNX Runtime session. On Arm CPUs it is 2-3x faster
than ONNX Runtime for these models (SCRFD 42 ms vs 99 ms, ArcFace ResNet100
57 ms vs 96 ms per face on an Apple M1, fp32 in both) with identical
outputs, at the cost of more resident memory. fp16 weights and arithmetic
are available as a setting (2x faster again) but MNN 3.6 returned wrong
outputs for some inputs of the ArcFace and CLIP text models with them, so
fp32 is the default; the text tower stays on ONNX Runtime by default, which
is faster than MNN fp32 for it.

- sessions/mnn/__init__.py: MnnSession over MNN's Module API (explicit input
  and output names, static shapes, serialised inference, precision and
  thread settings)
- sessions/mnn/convert.py: converts the ONNX Immich already downloads with
  MNN's converter in a subprocess (it keeps several copies of the graph while
  optimising) and stores the ONNX input/output signature next to the model,
  since MNN keeps neither the output order nor symbolic dimensions
- ModelFormat.MNN, chosen by default for facial recognition models (and CLIP
  text models with MACHINE_LEARNING_MNN_TEXTUAL) when MACHINE_LEARNING_MNN is
  set and the mnn package is installed; the model is converted on first load
  next to the ONNX file and regenerated when the precision setting changes.
  Models that fail to convert fall back to ONNX like the other formats. The
  face recogniser runs one face per call on MNN, which keeps its input shape
  fixed (MNN caches activations per shape)
- settings: MACHINE_LEARNING_MNN, MNN_PRECISION (FP32/FP16), MNN_THREADS,
  MNN_TEXTUAL
- pyproject: mnn extra (onnxruntime + mnn), tests for format selection, the
  session and the converter's checks

